# Layer Responsibilities

## API Layer

The API layer is responsible for interacting with external clients.

Responsibilities include:

- HTTP endpoints
- Request validation
- Authentication
- Authorization
- Response generation
- API documentation

Examples

- FastAPI Routers
- Request DTOs
- Response DTOs

The API layer contains no business logic.

---

## Application Layer

The Application layer coordinates business use cases.

Responsibilities include:

- Use case execution
- Workflow orchestration
- Service coordination
- Transaction boundaries
- Validation
- Calling domain services
- Coordinating infrastructure services

Examples

- Chat Service
- Document Service
- Workflow Service
- Agent Service

The Application layer defines interfaces that are implemented by Infrastructure.

---

## Domain Layer

The Domain layer contains the core business logic.

Responsibilities include:

- Entities
- Value Objects
- Domain Services
- Business Rules
- Domain Interfaces
- Business Policies

Examples

- Document
- Agent
- Workflow
- Tool
- ExecutionState

The Domain layer has no dependencies on external frameworks.

---

## Infrastructure Layer

The Infrastructure layer contains technology-specific implementations.

Responsibilities include:

- Firestore Repository
- Qdrant Client
- OpenSearch Client
- Gemini Client
- Vertex AI Integration
- Google Cloud Storage
- MCP Clients
- External APIs

Infrastructure implements interfaces defined by higher layers.

---

# Dependency Rule

Dependencies always point inward.

```text
FastAPI
     │
     ▼
Application
     │
     ▼
Domain

Infrastructure
     │
     └──────────────► Implements Interfaces
```

The Domain layer must never depend upon:

- FastAPI
- Firestore
- LangGraph
- Gemini SDK
- Vertex AI SDK
- Qdrant Client
- OpenSearch Client
- Cloud SDKs

